{
  "about": "Ruling 54's final image evaluation: the twenty-four pictures of labels_v2.json, their scene labels mapped to the two-way question, written by bench/images/labels_v3.py before any model was asked under it (21 Oct 2026). labels.json and labels_v2.json are not edited. Not edited after the run: a label found wrong afterwards is reported as a disagreement.",
  "mapping": "scene: owner_owes -> commitment, owed_to_owner -> commitment, reference -> reference, unsure -> unsure. Every other field is labels_v2.json's, as it stands (expected_waiting_on included, kept as a record: the photo path no longer writes a waiting-on label).",
  "conventions": "expected_gate, ocr_keywords, expected_tasks: as in labels.json. scene: what the picture represents, one of owner_owes (the owner promised something to a specific person, or owes an action by a date), owed_to_owner (a specific person promised the owner something, or the owner is waiting on them), reference (information worth keeping, no promise in either direction), or unsure where the label-writer would not commit. expected_tasks are judged only where the scene answer sends the picture to extraction. expected_waiting_on (owed_to_owner only): what the owner is waiting for, from whom, by when. mirrored: two pairs with matching wording and the opposite direction. Two names in the ruling's examples were already in fixtures (Priya, Marcus) and are replaced by Ines and Teodor; the wording is otherwise the ruling's.",
